  "description": "An ATX v1.1 credential issued by the primary authority (did:opena2a:authority:opena2a.org) at trustLevel 3, whose signed root-first issuerChain names the partner authority (did:opena2a:authority:partner.example) and the primary authority, carrying two Ed25519 signatures over the same JCS(TBS) bytes: one by the primary authority's key (#key-1) and one by the partner authority's key (#key-1). The verifier trusts both authorities, publishes each key under its own DID, and requires trust level 3 (verifierState.requiredTrustLevel). Two distinct authorities have each produced a signature the verifier verifies itself, so the distinct signer-authority count of atx-spec core.md §1.3 step 7 is 2. Verifier MUST ACCEPT. This is the control for the four fixtures that carry the same credential with a different signature set and MUST REJECT: v1_1-cosigner-named-not-signed, v1_1-one-authority-threshold-keys, v1_1-one-key-under-two-dids and v1_1-own-key-labelled-as-cosigner.",
